hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16054","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, he said, Abu Aqil, meaning al-Thaqafi, Abd Allah ibn Aqil, narrated to us, Musa ibn al-Musayyab narrated to us, Salim ibn Abi al-Jad informed me, from Sabrah ibn Abi Fakih, he said, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Satan sat for the son of Adam on his paths, so he sat for him on the path of Islam, and said to him, do you accept Islam and leave your religion and the religion of your fathers and the fathers of your father. He said, so he disobeyed him and accepted Islam. Then he sat for him on the path of emigration, and said, do you emigrate and leave your land and your sky, and the parable of the emigrant is but like that of a horse in a tether. He said, so he disobeyed him and emigrated. He said, then he sat for him on the path of jihad, and said to him, it is the striving of soul and wealth, so you fight and are killed, and the wife is married, and the wealth divided. He said, so he disobeyed him and strove. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does that of them and dies, it is due upon Allah to admit him to Paradise, or is killed, it is due upon Allah, mighty and majestic, to admit him to Paradise, and if he drowns, it is due upon Allah to admit him to Paradise, or his mount throws him, it is due upon Allah to admit him to Paradise."
